# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: FI
# source: https://www.finlex.fi/fi/laki/ajantasa/1934/19340205
#   (Laki uskonnonvapaudesta / Laki vapaapäivistä; Finnish official holidays.
#   Local copy papers/holidays/fi_holidays.md.) Finnish AND Swedish are both
#   official languages, so each name carries both, "Finnish / Swedish". Movable
#   Midsummer/All Saints are Saturday-anchored: Juhannuspäivä = Saturday in
#   20–26 June (Sat on/before 26 Jun); Juhannusaatto = the preceding Friday
#   (Fri on/before 25 Jun); Pyhäinpäivä = Saturday in 31 Oct–6 Nov (Sat on/before
#   6 Nov). Jouluaatto and Juhannusaatto are de-facto national holidays.
# retrieved: 2026-07-21
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed
#
